terminal, open the menu and press Enter on Remove > Theme within 0.5 s: the row may still show from the previous answer and Enter only closes the menu"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"The menu re-runs the guards on each open but first draws the previous answers, about 0.5 s on the reference box, as for every guarded row (docs/menu.md, Guards). Removing the last theme from a terminal and opening Remove at once can still show Theme until the batch lands; Enter then runs the remover, which says nothing and exits. The PR and 390Z state this window; whether a maintainer wants a narrower one is a product question for all guarded rows, not this row.","refs":[{"id":"default/omarchy/omarchy-menu.jsonc","kind":"file","line":296},{"id":"SW-REQ-261003-390Z","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-JRW1","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Question: the first open after the last extra theme goes away can still show the row for about half a second","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Open Remove right after removing the last extra theme\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["bin/omarchy-theme-remove"],"scenario":"with ~/.config/omarchy/themes symlinked into a dotfiles repo holding theme mine, run omarchy theme remove mine: the theme is removed from the dotfiles repo although the menu offers nothing there"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"The helper lists nothing when ~/.config/omarchy/themes is itself a symlink, so the menu offers no theme there. `omarchy theme remove <name>` from a terminal takes the name as given and is unchanged by this PR, so it can still remove a theme directory inside a symlinked folder, which lives in the user's dotfiles. That predates the PR (the PR says the CLI is unchanged); whether the CLI should follow the helper is a separate question.","refs":[{"id":"bin/omarchy-theme-remove","kind":"file","line":19},{"id":"bin/omarchy-theme-removable","kind":"file","line":13},{"id":"SW-REQ-261003-390Z","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"low","title":"Question: should the terminal command also refuse a symlinked themes folder?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"omarchy theme remove through a symlinked themes folder\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"detail":"review.effects is absent (disclosure effects_unavailable): the analyzer covers C/C++ only, so call-path statements here come from reading the code. The PR's test and the behaviour harness run the real helper, remover and guard batch.","refs":[{"id":"review.effects.approximations","kind":"check"},{"id":"bin/omarchy-theme-remove","kind":"file","line":9}],"severity":"info","title":"Analysis bounds: no change-effects analysis for bash","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}}],"packageDigest":"sha256:7b8030383b335b4b4edbfc029f3dac2682a4275e1ebd42ee2df7e18f1f43e905","packageIdentity":"epkg-030a7a53b5eb0dd1743490e3ee907d2c2ab58caa22acd3b63d14d50733f668c7","riskAssessment":{"level":"medium","rationale":"A small change: one new 21-line helper, one changed line in the remover and one guard on the row, pinned by a twelve-home test and a behaviour comparison whose 8 differences are all classified intended with identical controls. Medium, not low, because 8 prevents_ready disclosures remain (the 8 unapproved compat findings), the scripts have no engine-measured code MC/DC, and the half-second stale-answer window is not measured live in this package. Not merge approval."},"schemaVersion":"reqproof.review-annotation.v1","suggestedTests":[{"forClaim":14,"rationale":"Measures the stale-answer window for this row in a running shell.","refs":[{"id":"default/omarchy/omarchy-menu.jsonc","kind":"file","line":296},{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-guards-test.sh","kind":"file","line":442}],"title":"Open Remove right after removing the last extra theme"},{"forClaim":15,"rationale":"Pins what the terminal command does where the menu offers nothing.","refs":[{"id":"bin/omarchy-theme-remove","kind":"file","line":19}],"title":"omarchy theme remove through a symlinked themes folder"}],"summary":"**What the PR does.** omacom/omarchy#14153 (head 9a160c1f) fixes #14150: on a machine with only the bundled themes, Remove > Theme ran a remover with nothing to offer and only closed the menu. The PR adds omarchy-theme-removable, which lists the themes the remover can remove (directories that are not symlinks or dot-directories, nothing in a symlinked folder) and exits nonzero when there are none. The row asks it as its when:, and the remover reads its list from it, as Update > Extra Themes does with omarchy-theme-extras.\n\n**Is the fix verified?** The audit run is clean (0 errors, 0 warnings). Test results are ingested and current: 56/56 passed; all 29 changed requirements are observed_pass; 25 obligation cells observed_pass, 34 not_linked. The behaviour-comparison harness and its 12 guard inputs have observed outcomes (13 passed). The helper and the remover are not code-MC/DC targets, so diffCoverage counts 0 changed decisions.\n\n**Compatibility.** All four compat sources ran. 8 unapproved findings (prevents_ready), all differential and classified intended against SW-REQ-261003-390Z: the row is hidden for an empty, missing, symlink-only, file-only, dot-only or symlinked themes folder, and next to a real theme the picker no longer offers .git. Controls (a copied, cloned, worktree or -n theme) are identical. test_diff, mcdc_diff and removed_behavior report none.\n\n**Questions for a human.** Approve or reject each compat finding. The first open after the last theme goes away can show the row for about half a second (as for every guarded row). Should the terminal command also refuse a symlinked themes folder (unchanged by this PR)?\n\n**Traceability.** All 18 changed files map to a requirement: the remove.theme row maps to SW-REQ-261003-390Z at row level, and the new helper (a bash script with no functions) by an exact file-level trace. No spec-gap candidate remains.\n\n**Not caused by this PR.** coverage_unmeasured, checks_skipped (by configuration) and effects_unavailable (bash) inform only.\n\n**Readiness** is not_assessed; next decision human_judgement (compat_changes_unapproved, 8 changes), reviewer authority. Nothing here is an approval."}
